[0.004, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Are the accounts we closed last quarter actually using the product?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 79s over 6 steps, 27,282 tokens, 17 observations gathered, 11 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Of the nine accounts closed won last quarter (2026-04-01 to 2026-06-30), only three — Globex, Hooli, and Wonka Industries — show measurable product usage (workspace-opened events) through 2026-09-23; the other six show no usage in the data available.  [hubspot.closed_won 18244053, posthog.event_trend f6437900]\r\n  No Slack discussion referencing adoption, churn risk, or stalled onboarding for any of the nine named accounts was found, indicating this gap has not yet surfaced as an internal concern.  [slack.search_messages fa730df4, slack.search_messages 9d101ed6, slack.search_messages fef7afbe]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Only 3 of 9 accounts closed last quarter show any product usage  (medium)\r\n    - Nine deals closed won between 2026-04-01 and 2026-06-30: Northwind Traders, Globex, Initech, Umbrella Industries, Hooli, Soylent Corp, Vandelay Industries, Wonka Industries, and Cyberdyne Systems.  [hubspot.closed_won 18244053]\r\n    - The 'workspace opened' event breakdown by organization for 2026-04-01 through 2026-09-23 contains only three organizations: Globex (731 events), Hooli (554 events), and Wonka Industries (804 events).  [posthog.event_trend f6437900, posthog.event_trend 46b8c3aa]\r\n    - The remaining six accounts closed in the same quarter — Northwind Traders, Initech, Umbrella Industries, Soylent Corp, Vandelay Industries, and Cyberdyne Systems — do not appear anywhere in the workspace-opened breakdown for the period, meaning no observed usage under this event for those accounts.  [hubspot.closed_won 18244053, posthog.ev"]
[0.000, "o", "ent_trend f6437900]\r\n  No corroborating signal from other product events, and HubSpot company records are missing for the silent accounts  (low)\r\n    - trial_started returned zero rows for the entire 2026-04-01 to 2026-09-23 window, so it cannot confirm or rule out usage for any account.  [posthog.event_trend df9fc907]\r\n    - checkout_started, broken down by organization, also returned zero rows for the same window, so it likewise cannot confirm or rule out usage.  [posthog.event_trend ec18cbaa]\r\n    - HubSpot company lookups for Northwind and Cyberdyne — two of the six silent accounts — returned no company records at all, so their absence from PostHog cannot be cross-checked against a CRM record either.  [hubspot.companies 96f6b9ba, hubspot.companies c0d45423]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] The six silent accounts are not using the product because they were never technically onboarded (e.g., no workspace or organizati"]
[0.000, "o", "on mapping created), rather than churn or disengagement.\r\n      No onboarding records, annotations, or Slack messages were found naming these accounts, so this cannot be confirmed against direct evidence — only inferred from absence of data across two independent sources (PostHog and HubSpot).\r\n  [contradicted] A recent deploy to acme/product broke usage tracking for the silent accounts around the time they closed.\r\n      acme/product's last push was 2026-07-16, after all nine deals closed (latest close 2026-06-30), and three of the nine accounts (Globex, Hooli, Wonka) show substantial usage volume in the same tracking pipeline across the same window, so a tracking break cannot explain why only six of nine accounts are silent while three are not.\r\n  [inconclusive] Slack conversations reveal awareness within the GTM team that certain closed accounts are stalled or not adopting the product.\r\n      Searches for 'churn usage closed won' and 'onboarding stalled' both returned only generic, unrelated GTM channel "]
[0.000, "o", "chatter (renewal paperwork, pricing one-pager requests, meeting scheduling) with no mention of adoption status for any named account. A further search naming all six silent accounts by name also returned only the same four unrelated messages. This indicates no visible internal discussion of the issue, not that the issue does not exist.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Verify the organization-to-account mapping in PostHog for Northwind Traders, Initech, Umbrella Industries, Soylent Corp, Vandelay Industries, and Cyberdyne Systems before concluding they are not using the product.\r\n      why: Six of nine newly closed accounts show zero usage events, but this could be a tracking/mapping gap rather than true non-adoption, and that distinction changes the appropriate response entirely.\r\n      [hubspot.closed_won 18244053, posthog.event_trend f6437900]\r\n  P1 Have Customer Success directly reach out to the six accounts with no observed workspace "]
[0.000, "o", "activity to confirm onboarding status.\r\n      why: No Slack or CRM evidence surfaced any internal discussion or record of these accounts' onboarding progress, so a direct check is the only way to distinguish stalled onboarding from a data visibility gap.\r\n      [slack.search_messages fa730df4, slack.search_messages 9d101ed6, slack.search_messages fef7afbe]\r\n  P2 Investigate why trial_started and checkout_started show zero events across the entire six-month window, even for accounts with confirmed workspace activity.\r\n      why: These two events returning entirely empty results across all organizations for six months suggests a possible instrumentation gap that limits visibility into the full usage funnel, not just for the accounts in question.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend df9fc907, posthog.event_trend ec18cbaa]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The absence of six accounts from the workspace-opened breakdown could reflect an organization-pr"]
[0.000, "o", "operty mapping gap in PostHog (e.g., the account name in HubSpot does not match the organization property in PostHog) rather than genuine non-usage. This was not ruled out.\r\n  - trial_started and checkout_started returning zero rows across the whole six-month window for all organizations, including the three known-active accounts, suggests these events may not be firing at all in this tenant's instrumentation, rather than genuinely having zero occurrences — a broader gap that limits what can be said about onboarding-stage behavior for any account.\r\n  - HubSpot company records could not be retrieved for Northwind or Cyberdyne, so it is unclear whether this is a data completeness issue in HubSpot itself, which would limit visibility into contract or contact details for these accounts beyond just usage.\r\n  - 2 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - 2 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and "]
[0.000, "o", "are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[3]: The searches only queried general terms and six unnamed accounts (not all nine named ones), so absence of hits doesn't confirm no discussion exists for all nine, and the 'not yet a\r\n- findings[1].claims[1]: The payload shows row_count 0 for checkout_started over that window, though breakdown_property returned null instead of 'organization' and measure was count not unique_users, a min\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - PostHog's organization breakdown for 'workspace opened' surfaced data for only 3 of 9 target accounts; whether the other 6 have zero usage or are simply not mapped to an 'organization' property could not be determined from the tools available.\r\n  - trial_started and checkout_started returned zero rows for the entire query window across all organizations, which may indicate these events are n"]
[0.001, "o", "ot instrumented for this tenant rather than truly zero occurrences.\r\n  - HubSpot company lookups for Northwind Traders and Cyberdyne Systems returned no records, despite both appearing as closed-won deals, indicating incomplete company-level records in HubSpot for at least some closed accounts.\r\n  - 4 of the 11 cited observation(s) returned no results (hubspot.companies, posthog.event_trend). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  1b8fbd36  github.list_repositories  eval://github__list_repositories\r\n  18244053  hubspot.closed_won  eval://hubspot__closed_won\r\n  96f6b9ba  hubspot.companies  eval://hubspot__companies\r\n  c0d45423  hubspot.companies  eval://hubspot__companies\r\n  f6437900  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  df9fc907  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  ec18cbaa  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r"]
